   "id": "fn-p010-1",
   "page": 10,
   "mark": "4",
   "text": "There is another advantage to draw the Young diagrams in rotated French notation.A transition from λkto λk+1 occurs when one keeps a box at any of the minima of rotated diagram. Putting a box at diﬀerent minima corresponds to diﬀerent diagrams at k + 1 level. Therefore the transition probabilities are denoted by µa where a is the position of a minimum. To ﬁnd µa we deﬁne two polynomials P(x) = Qn",
